+## Owner changes (Nov 9 evening)
+
+Requested by the owner in his own words ("I just want to see the picture", "it just clutters the Telegram", seven-leg parlays):
+
+- **One picture per ticket batch.** `send` delivers the PNG under the batch key with a short caption (`ticket_caption`: every ticket's legs with the stored price, the payout at those prices, the quote time; at most 1,024 characters, shortened rather than refused). No separate text message is sent. The exact full text is still stored in `deliveries.text`, `ticket_batches` and the archive. The `ticket-image:` receipt is recorded as the same Telegram message, so every later step (settlement, result notices, delivery alerts, `ticket_deliveries`) reads the receipts it read before.
+- **Fallbacks.** If the picture cannot be rendered, the earlier text-then-image path runs unchanged (the ticket still arrives as text; the failed image receipt alerts as before). A batch whose text was already sent by the earlier release keeps the earlier path for its image.
+- **Quiet health states.** `source_unavailable_or_stale` and `missing_due_forecasts` (`QUIET_HEALTH`) are no longer sent to the chat: they clear within minutes and their text meant nothing to the reader. They remain in the preflight report, the snapshot and the trigger observations. Every other alert (delivery review required, result notice not delivered, store identity, settlement) is unchanged.
+- **Up to seven legs** (`MAX_LEGS = 7`). The card renders seven-leg tickets; the picture still shows the first three tickets and the caption lists all of them.
+- **One game card per game** (`telegram.format_batch`, key `pregame-2`): a re-issued forecast or a moved line no longer sends the same game again; a changed start time or a changed recommended pick does.
+
+Not changed here: the review instructions (`SKILL.md`), the automation schedule, selection rules, settlement, stores. Tested in a Linux copy of this checkout (Python 3.10): the five test files that import the changed modules, 227 passed. Not run: the full backend suite, the release venv, a real Telegram send.
